Proliferative breast diseases with atypical hyperplasia includes atypical ductal hyperplasia and atypical lobular hyperplasia.
Atypical hyperplasia is pathologic diagnosis, usually found as an incidental on biopsy of mammographic abnormalities or
breast lumps. These lesions have some, but not all, features of ductal carcinoma in situ or lobular carcinoma in situ. These
lesions, especially if multifocal are associated with a significantly increased risk of breast cancer. 
Mia’s breast cyst and the fibrocystic disease are both nonproliferative lesions from category one and does not confer an increased risk of
breast cancer.
(Option C) Most women with breast cancer do not have a family history; however, having one or more first-degree relatives or second-degree
relatives on the same side of family with breast cancer is associated with increased risk of breast cancer. Mia, with one first-degree relative
(mother) diagnosed with breast cancer after the age of 50, is at slightly increased risk of breast cancer (1.8 times the normal population).
Despite being modest, family history can play a role as cause of breast cancer.
(Option B) Many studies have shown that tobacco smoking may be associated with an increased risk of breast cancer. While there are some
limitations to the evidence, studies have been generally consistent in supporting a link between tobacco smoking and increased risk of breast,
particularly in women who have started smoking when they were younger or have started smoking many years before having their first child.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2023','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-a1c738f39cf4","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"649d9c1eb630e5eab087","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":145,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
