 B) Analgesics can be given for pain control. It is not a priority before debridement, swabs and antibiotics.\n(Option C) In the presence of an infection/inflammation, lateral, antero-posterior, and oblique X-ray views of both feet should be performed with the X-ray request specifying the\nanatomical location of the ulcer and mentioning the possibility of underlying osteomyelitis, diabetic arthropathy, and gas formation. However, it can be performed after more\nimportant steps (debridement, swabs, and antibiotics) have been taken.\n (Option D) MRI is indicated if osteomyelitis is suspected based on the following:\nUlcers unresponsive to antibiotic therapy\nProbing the wound results in bone being touched\nBone is visible in the base of the wound\nX-ray suggest bone involvement\nIn this scenario, MRI is not a priority in management.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","antibiotic","antimicrobial","diabetes","duration","management","therapy","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"very_high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"1a4be3cbfd0e7bba192170445d5d3635ec14f7ff","duplicate_group_id":"exact-1a4be3cbfd0e","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b64e8a32e89fd0d639f9","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":159,"source_qid":"1134"}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_ass