porosis in AN. Peak bone mass is generally acquired during adolescence and young adulthood, which\nfrequently coincides with the onset of AN. The peak bone mass acquired by a patient with AN depends on the time of onset and duration of\nthe eating disorder, the degree of nutritional depletion, and changes in body composition.\nThe AN-associated osteoporosis is different from that found in the typical postmenopausal state. In AN, patients have low serum levels of\nestrogen, androgens, IGF-1, and leptin. In addition, there are high levels of cortisol and normal serum levels of calcium, vitamin D, and\nparathyroid hormone.\nIn all patients with AN longer than 6 months, a bone mineral density (BMD) should be measured with dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry\n(DEXA). For patients who continue to suffer episodes of AN, a follow-up test should be done every 2 years.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","drug","duration","therapy","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"49c6d68aa70807459cc415ffbf5c9a8b88349a1e","duplicate_group_id":"exact-49c6d68aa708","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"15abcb4128ac53e97141","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":178,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visu