stered unless bacterial infections are suspected after initial\ninvestigations such as full blood count (FBC), chest X-ray, etc.\n(Option B) This patient has a normal blood pressure and does not seem to be in urgent need for fluid resuscitation. However, it may be\nconsidered if further studies indicate otherwise.\n(Options D and E) ABG is often the first-line investigation to exclude hypoxia as the most common cause of post-operative\ndelirium/confusion. A chest X-ray is indicated for evaluation and workup of conditions such as atelectasis, pneumonia, or pulmonary\nembolism if the patient is found to be hypoxic/hypoxemic. Again, obtaining an arterial sample for ABG can be difficult in this patient and\nshould be attempted once the patient is easier to deal with.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","antibiotic","drug","management","prophyl","resuscitation","therapy","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"very_high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"7afedebf2784af8e345ebd29229af236fc31a818","duplicate_group_id":"exact-7afedebf2784","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"8f0e308b4dbbcf094582","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":282,"source_qid":"1131"}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,curre