Atypical antipsychotics such as risperidone, olanzapine or ziprasidone are second-line choices that can be used as alternatives; however, in
the presence of extrapyramidal symptoms, they should be use in preference to haloperidol. Intravenous diazepam (not an option) is the
medication of choice if alcohol withdrawal or delirium tremens are suspected from the history and clinical findings.
NOTE - Pharmacological therapy should only be considered in a delirious person with severe behavioral disturbance and/or severe emotional
disturbance if their behavior threatens their own safety or the safety of others, is likely to interfere with essential medical or nursing care, or
if the disturbance is causing significant distress
(Option A) Although the patient is febrile, antibiotics should not be administered unless bacterial infections are suspected after initial
investigations such as full blood count (FBC), chest X-ray, etc.
(Option B) This patient has a normal blood pressure and does not seem to be in urgent need for fluid resuscitation. However, it may be
considered if further studies indicate otherwise.
(Options D and E) ABG is often the first-line investigation to exclude hypoxia as the most common cause of post-operative
delirium/confusion. A chest X-ray is indicated for evaluation and workup of conditions such as atelectasis, pneumonia, or pulmonary
embolism if the patient is found to be hypoxic/hypoxemic. Again, obtaining an arterial sample for ABG can be difficult in this patient and
should be attempted once the patient is easier to deal with.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2023','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"1131","duplicate_group_id":"exact-7afedebf2784","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"8f0e308b4dbbcf094582","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":282,"source_qid":"1131"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
